WEBVTT

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.200
Is this Nogoro-kun?{AMS: ep3 22:38}

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.370
The opponent for the practice game that you wanted has been decided.{AMS: ep3 22:44}

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.160
Even within Kanagawa, they're strong and famous:{AMS: ep3 22:49}

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.110
Yokohama Teijin High School.{AMS: ep3 22:53}

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.250
How about it, Nogoro-kun?{AMS: ep3 22:56}

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.800
It's perfect.{AMS: ep3 23:00}

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.280
Since we're playing anyway, the stronger the opponent, the more fired up we'll be!{AMS: ep3 23:01} {I would like to split it if you think it's approiate}{AMS: it's consistent with the previous episode}

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.050
Short!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.320
Next! Second!

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.130
Hey, hey, are you serious?

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.770
Isn't this team, like, incredibly strong?

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.630
How are we supposed to play an exhibition game against such a strong team?{AMS: "is it we're able to play a practice game with" to "are we supposed to play an exhibition game against"}

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.350
Who knows?

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:38.140
But apparently the advisor, Yamada,
has connections from when he used to work here.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.810
That English teacher, Perry.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.350
So, thanks again, Minegishi-sensei.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.820
If it's you asking, then it's no problem!{AMS: "your request" to "you asking"}

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.190
It seems like my students are ready to go.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:10.000
Well then, let's have a good game today!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.310
Manager!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.900
What's up with this? Scheduling a game so suddenly?

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.600
It'll be a problem. This afternoon we have a game with Kawajitsu.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.690
Now, now, don't be like that.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.540
It couldn't be helped, could it?
After all, it was a request from an old friend.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.900
But... Seishuu is a school that has never played an official game before.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:42.050
There's no way that it'd be a real game with us playing a low-level team like them.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.880
That's why I scheduled the game before Kawajitsu...

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.150
as a warmup game. 

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.090
Take it easy on them.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.550
WHAT!?

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.990
What do you mean you're not members of the baseball team?

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.770
There's no what or how about it.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:08.930
We're only here to see Shigeno's pitiful face when he loses the bet.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:12.940
The bet?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.120
Yeah, he's the one who started it.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:20.960
All we have to do is stand there and do nothing.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.580
If he can prove to us that he can win a game by himself,
without having to rely on anyone else,

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.300
we're supposed to join the baseball team.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.760
Same with you first-years?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.190
Y-Yeah...

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.720
With that promise, we were forced to come here today.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.580
Are you serious, Nogoro-kun?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.760
Yeah.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:52.140
Because if I can't, then these guys won't join.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:57.400
Well, they look strong but if everything depends on this,
then I guess I'll just have to do it.{AMS: "it comes down to this" to "everything depends on this"}

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.750
<i>Darling! You're so cool!</i>

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.960
{Um...}Shall we start soon?

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.410
Let's have a good game!

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.380
Where are you going to stand?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.820
Who cares where?

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.080
We're not going to need to catch it, right?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.430
Oh... right.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.850
That's right.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.570
Hey, hey, look at that.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.800
Isn't that catcher a girl?

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:50.290
That pitcher can throw pretty fast,

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.750
but it's within our level, isn't it?

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:00.930
Play ball!

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:07.350
Do your best, darling!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.360
What are you staring at?

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.360
<i>This catcher really is a girl!</i>

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.240
S-Strike!

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.550
Strike!

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.470
<i>I don't care if it's a famous school or not...</i>

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.970
<i>They're weaker than Kaido is!</i>

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.560
Strike! Batter out!

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.980
W-What the hell is this guy?

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.610
<i>Just you watch!</i>

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:01.950
<i>Until I get to play against Kaido, I'm not gonna stop!</i>

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.120
What's going on here?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.620
I wasn't told about this.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.460
Why is a guy like this... at Seishuu?

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.530
Strike! Batter out!

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.090
Change!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.640
Why is such a monster there!? 

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.490
Wonderful!

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.060
Wonderful, Nogoro-kun!

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.500
It's the first time I've seen such a fastball in my life!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.560
You really are amazing, darling!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.400
Well... this is just the normal me.{I'm just living regularly!}

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:42.710
{-Missing Translation-}{AMS: TLC couldn't make it out}

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.740
Wonderful!

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:44.120
Yeah! {Added by Timer}

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.080
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: TLC couldn't make it out}

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.080
{- Missing Translation -}{AMS: TLC couldn't make it out}

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:51.640
<i>This is... a bit harder than I imagined it would be. </i>

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.960
You guys agreed to a useless bet, didn't you?

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:04.010
Before he came here, do you know where Shigeno used to go?

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.140
Kaido! He went to Kaido!

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:23.100
Just to play against Kaido, this guy transferred to our school.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:35.470
Whoa! Wonderful! Amazing!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.510
Darling! That was great!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.490
Darling, you're incredible! {added by timer tlc}

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.490
Incredible!{I have no freaking clue why this doesn't overlap...}

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.130
<i>There's no way you can win!</i>

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.350
<i>I'm telling you there's no way you'll be able to win against Kaido by yourself!</i>

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.190
<i>Why not?</i>

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.400
<i>Why not!?{sangofe: probably have ""Why not!?", no? Or "It's not why not!" or something...}</i>

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.560
<i>To come to Seishuu, which has no people that have played baseball before, and challenge Kaido...</i>

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.030
<i>There's a limit to these kinds of things you know!</i>

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:06.740
<i>Why didn't you transfer to someplace better!?</i>

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.470
<i>It's because it's Seishuu that it's okay.</i>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.580
<i>I don't need someone who knows a lot about baseball.</i>

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.630
<i>I want to find out...</i>

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:23.090
<i>how far I can go... with my own strength.</i>

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:32.860
<i>Man...</i>

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:35.850
<i>such a bothersome story.</i>

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.070
Out!

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.730
Strike! Batter out!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.780
Strike! Batter out!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.740
H-He just struck 13 people out in a row!?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.000
Just hit the ball and get on base!

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:44.500
Out!

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.190
The third strike bunt failed!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.210
Strike! Batter out!

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:09.030
H-He's amazing.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:12.990
We could seriously just stand there and do nothing.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.990
What nonsense.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.150
Stop joking around.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:23.540
I won't join the baseball team, even if you win it this way.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.220
What's "nonsense"?

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.430
Are you trying to pretend that there's no bet?

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:34.800
This doesn't represent a simulation of a real game.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.250
What?

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.230
It's the catcher! The catcher!

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.680
She's catching them now,

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:45.400
but when we get to the real games,
who's going to be able to catch those pitches?

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:52.440
Rely on one of the first-years next year... or something?

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.730
Do you really think someone like that is going to come to our school?

00:11:55.730 --> 00:12:00.480
If you can't find someone to catch them,
you're going to have to seal those fastballs.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:03.620
And if that happens, of course they're going to hit the pitches.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:06.380
We're going to end up embarrassed and lose!

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:17.260
This game isn't anything like you said it would be!

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:24.190
Man... you guys are so noisy.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:27.150
What're you making such a huge deal about?

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:31.440
Fine then. I'll be the catcher for you!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.400
Fuji?

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:46.380
This is a free fansub.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:46.380
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.330
I'll catch the balls you pitch.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.720
There's no way that you'll be able to catch such fast pitching!

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.000
Just quit! Just quit!

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.480
Since you can't do anything,
you're going to get seriously hurt.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.290
WHAT!?

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.970
I get it.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.440
Go ahead and try, Fuji.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.420
Are you serious?

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:15.450
Yeah.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.810
Just like this guy says,

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:22.410
if Shimizu's catching,
then this game doesn't represent a simulation.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:27.060
Sooner or later, someone's going to have to be the catcher.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.380
If you're going to volunteer,

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.340
then I'm happy to hear that.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.040
Strike!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:40.650
WIll you be okay, Fuji?

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:43.360
His fastballs are really strong!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.170
I have to do it, don't I?

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:50.230
I can't let you get hurt any longer.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.440
Every time you got back to the bench,
you were icing your left hand, weren't you?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.120
Don't tell me because of this...

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:02.830
It's not like that.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:07.530
I'm just trying to enjoy this thing called baseball.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.130
All right! Let's go!

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.800
Damn it! One more time!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.610
All right, let's go!

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.800
<i>There's no way he can catch it.</i>

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.640
Strike! Out!

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.280
Three outs! Change!

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.860
I guess I can't catch it.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.200
But if you throw the ball right at me,
I should be able to manage somehow.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.330
Even if I get hurt, I won't let it get by.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.670
Just like before, throw it with everything you've got.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:53.920
Fuji.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.580
You just keep quiet and keep your mitt in the middle.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.640
Leave the rest to me.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.270
Play!

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:12.230
<i>Keep quiet and keep my mitt in the middle?</i>

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:25.700
S-Strike!

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.730
S-Strike!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.910
H-He caught it?

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:34.960
No, rather than him catching it, it was more like that guy threw it to the spot where Fuji was holding his mitt.

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:38.170
No way! That was just luck, right?

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.100
Strike!

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.760
<i>This guy...</i>

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:48.770
<i>Even at this speed he can do something like that, too?</i>

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:03.430
All right! You'll hit it! You can hit it!

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.330
He's throwing it to one spot only: straight down the middle!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.830
Choke up on the bat and hit it!

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:11.370
Will my darling be all right?

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:15.340
As expected of the famous Teijin.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.340
Even with Nogoro-kun's pitching,

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:21.000
with a catcher that can only catch in the middle,

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.900
there's nothing we can do about them catching up to it.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:29.010
Third!

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.060
W-What's going on?

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:41.400
Lucky, lucky!

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.150
I don't know what's going on,
but there's no outs and a runner on first!{AMS: "it's a no out to first base!" to "but there's no outs and a runner on first"}

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.850
Hey! What're you picking it up for?

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.160
Well, but...

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:54.130
We don't have to cooperate with him at all!

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.130
He said he can win by himself,

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.520
so make him go get it by himself!

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:02.040
He's right.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:02.550
Yeah.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:09.700
<i>Can you really make a baseball team with guys like these?{timed after "oi", "oi" on purpose, since it's not in subs -sangofe}</i>

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.430
<i>That bastard.</i>

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:16.830
<i>I knew this from the beginning, </i>

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.150
<i>but the fact that he's being so uncooperative,</i>

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:20.070
<i>it makes me angry!{sangofe: "pisses me off" would be more appropriate here}</i>

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.940
Third, again!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.550
Oh, no!

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:33.080
Before I knew it the glove kind of just moved!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:35.660
Over here! Throw it to first!

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:37.480
No...

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:40.750
if there's no outs and a runner on first, then the only place to throw it... {i don't think it's a good idea to split it}

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.010
is over there.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:42.460
What!?

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.720
Huh? There's no one there!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.640
How uncool!

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.680
All right! Go around! Go around!

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.600
Hurry up, outfielders!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.850
How pathetic! 

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:59.800
We just got a two-run home run!

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.730
Tashiro!

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.270
Quit fooling around!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.740
You knew no one was there and threw it to second on purpose!

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:15.730
I won't tell you to cooperate...

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:20.040
but don't get in the way of other people's hard work!

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.120
Leave him alone.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.090
He's actually lonely.

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:30.930
He's just a lonely kid who pulled a little 
prank because he wanted attention, right?

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:34.870
Okay, okay...

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.670
That just means I'll have to change the way I do things.

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:43.720
Has he... played baseball before?

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:48.500
The way he caught the ball and threw it...

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:52.690
It seems like he's played it before.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.960
Hey, hey, you're in the way!

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.470
O-Out!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.640
I'm definitely going to get you to play baseball!

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:36.080
Bottom of the seventh, one run difference, one out, huh?

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:41.030
We have to at least tie it up, or we'll definitely lose.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:47.490
If Shigeno can't do something, it's all over.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:52.930
Ball!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:58.390
<i>Damn! So, they're going to keep throwing balls, huh?</i>

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.370
He did it!

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:14.810
Out!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.000
Damn it!

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:28.620
It's over, huh?

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.610
And now, I'm 100% sure that we're going to lose.

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:35.760
Which means we no longer have to join the baseball team!

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:36.600
Tashiro! 

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:39.320
Open your eyes, Fuji.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:42.810
What'll it be like if you start baseball now?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.460
Next year we'll have to study for our college exams.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:53.330
We're already in our second year of high school. What's the point in starting baseball now?

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:54.030
Right?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.840
Y-Yeah...

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:58.990
No one is being tricked into playing.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.530
Strike!

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:03.850
I don't get it...

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.250
I don't get it, but...

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:11.610
When I first saw Shigeno's pitching,
I was so amazed it gave me goosebumps.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:16.250
Pro baseball... I haven't watched it a whole lot or anything.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:20.210
But to know that someone could throw an object so fast,

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.980
it made my hair stand on end.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.200
And...

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:30.110
the fact that a person who's in the same year as us can do that...

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.810
I was seriously amazed!

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:35.280
Fuji...

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.610
So what about it?

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:43.450
{Oh!}Nice batting!

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:46.120
The softball girl got a hit!

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:53.240
It's fine if you guys don't feel anything from watching that.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:22:01.010
But I'm sick of just sitting there in class not doing anything.

00:22:12.340 --> 00:22:13.030
Play!

00:22:16.490 --> 00:22:23.700
<i>Just from catching 30 of Shigeno's pitches;
I don't have that much strength anymore in my left hand...</i>

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:27.660
Strike!

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:30.120
<i>But...</i>

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.200
<i>in exchange for the pain, every time I catch one of his pitches,</i>

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:37.870
<i>it feels like I receive some amazing energy from him.</i>

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:48.980
<i>And... beyond his energy, I can feel it!</i>

00:22:56.530 --> 00:22:57.320
It got through!

00:22:58.240 --> 00:23:00.490
<i>If I'm out on the field with him...</i>

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:05.890
<i>I feel like I'll be able to see something even more amazing!</i>

00:24:40.570 --> 00:24:44.880
Even though everyone else's feelings are changing, Tashiro continues to fight it.

00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:46.970
What's the reason for you hating baseball so much?

00:24:47.580 --> 00:24:52.310
And then to us, the advisor, Yamada, gives us his conditions to approve the baseball team.

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.070
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.070 --> 00:24:55.710
Our Field.

00:24:55.710 --> 00:24:57.900
Run to the stage of your dreams!
